    "verdict": "mostly_artefact",
    "explanation": "At every append fraction measured \u2014 append_05 gap=0.538 (map=0.419 vs vector=0.958), append_20 gap=0.455 (map=0.395 vs vector=0.849), append_50 gap=0.339 (map=0.364 vs vector=0.703) \u2014 the map-space overlap is well below the vector-space overlap for the same 3000 base rows at k=20. A base row's own 256-d vector never moves when other rows are appended (base_vectors_moved_by_append=0.0); what moves, and moves far less than the map does, is which OTHER rows count as its true nearest neighbours. AC5's control shows this comparison is not just reporting near-1.0 by construction: a same-size, deliberately concentrated append drops vector overlap to 0.884 against append_05's 0.958. So the map's rearrangement at every fraction tested is mostly a projection artefact, not the data changing underneath it."
